SplitMind patch 0010 for OpenConnector v1.9.2.
The oauth-flow-service test "stores the token returned by a provider OAuth runtime"
hard-codes expiresAt 2026-10-30, a date that has expired, so the test fails on any
run after it. This makes the expiry one hour from now. Candidate for upstream.
Upstream issue: not filed yet.

From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SplitMind <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(oauth): use a relative expiry in the provider runtime token test

The fixture's expiresAt was the fixed date 2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z. Once that date
passed, the stored credential counted as expired and the test failed. The expiry is
now computed as one hour from Date.now(), and the assertion uses the same value.

---
diff --git a/src/oauth/oauth-flow-service.test.ts b/src/oauth/oauth-flow-service.test.ts
index 6b7366e6..435f2ffb 100644
--- a/src/oauth/oauth-flow-service.test.ts
+++ b/src/oauth/oauth-flow-service.test.ts
@@ -1262,6 +1262,7 @@ describe("OAuthFlowService", () => {
   });
 
   it("stores the token returned by a provider OAuth runtime", async () => {
+    const expiresAt = new Date(Date.now() + 60 * 60 * 1000).toISOString();
     let callbackParameters: Record<string, string> | undefined;
     let callbackQuery: string | undefined;
     let callbackState: string | undefined;
@@ -1275,7 +1276,7 @@ describe("OAuthFlowService", () => {
             accessToken: "provider-access-token",
             refreshToken: "provider-access-token",
             tokenType: "Bearer",
-            expiresAt: "2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z",
+            expiresAt,
             providerSecret: { inventory: "provider-owned" },
             metadata: { permissions: "read,write" },
           };
@@ -1301,7 +1302,7 @@ describe("OAuthFlowService", () => {
       authType: "oauth2",
       accessToken: "provider-access-token",
       refreshToken: "provider-access-token",
-      expiresAt: "2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z",
+      expiresAt,
       providerSecret: { inventory: "provider-owned" },
       metadata: { permissions: "read,write" },
     });
